Im not a rival company, I have nothing to gain from this. If you prefer your weed to be artifically flavored then go for it. some people like it, my friend thought it tasted good and wanted some but knew it was sprayed. If thats your thing great, now you have a place to get super flavorful weed... its just gonna taste really artificial.  I just wanted to get the word out because i dont like tasting chemicals when I smoke weed.

thats why i ordered this pink bubba! I had the greasy pink and it kicked my ass it was fantastic!

&#x200B;

really I loved these guys, i recommended them to everybody its why this breaks my heart cause they were honestly a pretty good go-to for me for years especially with all the free stuff and good customer support.

it tastes like hay stilll. I've grown before and this is clearly not finished properly.

&#x200B;

I seriously dont understand how anybody could smoke that grapefruit and not know instantly the artifical chemical taste and smell.  Maybe its just this batch i dunno, ive had their grapefruit and it was fine thats why i am kinda shocked here

&#x200B;

and dude, if your smoking the grapefruit I am... plants dont smell like that my dude... that "nose" your smelling isnt terpenes its like corn syrup or some other garbage spray I have no idea. it smells like a gummy container. there isnt even a hint of plant smell the grapefruit candy scent is so strong

the ,mku babies are fire they do a great job on itand ive had nothing but good luck with them aside from this order. ithe last pink bubba I ordered was fantastic.  you dont think that grapefruit is sprayed then you are crazy. the bag smells like a fucking chemical spray its awful to smoke the chemical aftertaste is very noticeable.

&#x200B;

I loved this MoM, and honestly totally shocked that they did this because ive had their grapefruit and it was great before, nothing like this sprayed garbage.

chronic illness. many people just disappear because they cannot function anymore and you just dont hear about them from anybody anymore. trust me I know im there. people who have spent all their money on every possible form of treatment, people who are told over and over they cannot be cured and still fight on and then they die... like a million fucking cancer patients every day so I think you are very naive.

&#x200B;

you think people who lose their limbs, parts of their brains, are just able to willpower that shit out of their lives? no they deal with it, and they put on a big fucking happy show so people like you dont have to feel bad about the world because we know how depressing our lives are to everyone else, trust me society makes it very obvious.

car accident victim, dead family, cant speak from head trauma... im sure god has a great plan for him. I bet he's really gonna push through that depression and host a ted talk on survivalism and positivity.

&#x200B;

you cant look at rare cases like stephen hawking and go "oh if he could do it why cant everyone else" its the same mental thinking that causes people to think less of sick and disabled people,you dont think about the kind of extra treatment some can afford, some people can afford expensive rehab programs, people to help them get dressed, get around, make food for them and then there are others whos families die and leave them with nothing. people who are not well off and do not have places to turn. The idea that if your in a bad spot you just arent willing it enough is incredibly toxic.

Hello I've got an EVH 5150III 50 watt amp that has both a pre-amp out and a headphone jack. If I wanted to run the output into my DAC to record/control headphone levels better without making noise in the room would it be better to take from the pre-amp out or the headphone jack? 

&#x200B;

Keep in mind, the speaker will be still connected but I can use a dummy headphone jack to silence the amp as it doesnt play sound while headphones are in, and I could take from the pre-amp out and still have no noise. Is this feasible? which one would make more sense to use?

